fidelity:
  divergences: >-
    The formalization states Theorem 3.5 directly against the full G-point's
    own Gh1,Gh2,Gh3 (rather than a separate "G-triple" object that forgets
    the fourth generator), and states Corollary 3.6 directly on a G-point.
    This is a strictly stronger packaging of the same underlying facts (a
    G-point always yields the weaker G-triple by forgetting one field), not
    a different theorem. The divisor classification's (D1) is proved as the
    polynomial-level statement Pi | qp K, which is stronger than and implies
    the paper's literal "every root of e over K-bar" phrasing without
    requiring an IsAlgClosed K hypothesis.

