README
# Jacobian Conjecture: four manuscripts

**Website:** https://supermindai.github.io/Jacobian-Conjecture/

This repository contains four self-contained research manuscripts by
**SuperMind** on the two-dimensional Jacobian conjecture.  The manuscript date
is August 3, 2026.  Each paper includes its own LaTeX source, bibliography, and
any reproducibility material needed for its computer-assisted components.

The two-dimensional Jacobian conjecture remains open.  These papers establish
bounded or conditional structural results; none claims a complete proof or a
counterexample.

## Papers

1. **Projection potentials and Lyashko--Looijenga rigidity for plane Keller
   maps.**  Develops projection-potential identities, excludes the
   zero-potential wall, and obtains the bounded consequence
   \(b_1\geq 9\).
   [PDF](https://supermindai.github.io/Jacobian-Conjecture/publication/01-projection-potentials-and-ll-rigidity.pdf) ·
   [essay](https://supermindai.github.io/Jacobian-Conjecture/papers/01-projection-potentials.html) ·
   [source](manuscripts/01-projection-potentials-ll-rigidity/)
2. **Singularity budgets for rational one-place curves and plane Keller
   maps.**  Proves \(N\leq 2R+2\) and the page-density inequality
   \((d-3a)R\leq a+1\) under the stated one-component hypothesis.
   [PDF](https://supermindai.github.io/Jacobian-Conjecture/publication/02-one-place-curves-and-page-density.pdf) ·
   [essay](https://supermindai.github.io/Jacobian-Conjecture/papers/02-singularity-budgets.html) ·
   [source](manuscripts/02-one-place-curves-page-density/)
3. **Common pencils and Suzuki saturation for affine-disjoint nonproper
   components of plane Keller maps.**  Establishes the common-pencil and
   Suzuki-saturation structure and excludes the exact clean nodal-cubic
   support considered in the paper.
   [PDF](https://supermindai.github.io/Jacobian-Conjecture/publication/03-disjoint-components-and-suzuki-pencils.pdf) ·
   [essay](https://supermindai.github.io/Jacobian-Conjecture/papers/03-common-pencils.html) ·
   [source](manuscripts/03-disjoint-components-suzuki-pencils/)
4. **The degree of a possible counterexample to the plane Jacobian conjecture
   is at least 125.**  Closes the two remaining degree-pair exceptions in the
   cited reduction through exact characteristic-zero and finite-field
   certificates.
   [PDF](https://supermindai.github.io/Jacobian-Conjecture/publication/04-plane-jacobian-degree-125.pdf) ·
   [essay](https://supermindai.github.io/Jacobian-Conjecture/papers/04-degree-125.html) ·
